    "title": "Improvements made to on-time performance calculations on 26th January 2024",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-02T09:59:12Z",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">On the<strong>&nbsp;26th of Jan 2024</strong>, the following improvements were deployed to the algorithm which is responsible for calculating all departure times in ABOD.</p><p><br></p><ol><li><strong dir=\"ltr\">Stop re-entry recalculation of departures&nbsp;</strong>– This improvement will ensure that the last known GPS ping from a vehicle is used when calculating departure times. This improvement will benefit scenarios where a vehicle enters a stops radius, then leaves and then re-enters again. In this scenario, the last known GPS ping inside the radius, helping prevent any inaccurate early departures from being calculated.</li><li dir=\"ltr\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">Interpolation of departures&nbsp;</strong>– Where reasonable amount of data exists, departures will now be calculated for stops which have been skipped due to low GPS update frequency, allowing for more actuals to be calculated and improving the overall data completeness in ABOD.</li></ol>",
    "description_text": " On the 26th of Jan 2024, the following improvements were deployed to the algorithm which is responsible for calculating all departure times in ABOD.      Stop re-entry recalculation of departures – This improvement will ensure that the last known GPS ping from a vehicle is used when calculating departure times. This improvement will benefit scenarios where a vehicle enters a stops radius, then leaves and then re-enters again. In this scenario, the last known GPS ping inside the radius, helping prevent any inaccurate early departures from being calculated.  Interpolation of departures – Where reasonable amount of data exists, departures will now be calculated for stops which have been skipped due to low GPS update frequency, allowing for more actuals to be calculated and improving the overall data completeness in ABOD.  ",
